{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 7, :comments ["מִדְבַּר שֶׁקֶר תִּרְחָק — And if a case appears to you to be fraudulent and the witnesses are deceitful, yet you cannot refute them, distance yourself from that case and do not judge it at all. Nevertheless, if he is clear and righteous in the case — the judgment having already been concluded in his favor — do not kill him any further, since you have already accepted the witnesses and concluded the judgment without paying attention to this, up to the end, meaning: if you declared him righteous, I will not declare him righteous — and he is liable to death, as written: והאלהים אנה לידו."], :book :exodus, :voice :rashbam, :lang :en, :chapter 23, :notes {0 "The phrase עד לסוף is rendered hyper-literally 'up to the end'; its precise syntactic relationship to what precedes is uncertain and the passage may be textually difficult."}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-30T14:42:46.189463150Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}